y? But communication is crucial for pilots. Egocentric may be problematic.\n\nCandidate D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but arrogance and weak leadership may be problematic.\n\nWe need to make a recommendation. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate A, despite communication difficulty, still creates positive atmosphere and is 100% reliable, quick correct decisions, which are critical. The communication difficulty could be mitigated with training, whereas B and C have more severe interpersonal issues (nasty remarks, unfriendly). D's arrogance and weak leadership also problematic.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: we note that B and C have concerns, and we bring A as under-discussed candidate.\n\nProvide evidence: A quick correct decisions, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nExplain why still best: reliability and decision quality are top, positive atmosphere suggests crew cooperation, communication difficulty less severe than B's nasty remarks and C's unfriendly attitude.\n\nThus vote Candidate A.\n\nNow produce public message and metadata."}
